# Copy to .env before `docker compose up` (.env is gitignored):
#   copy .env.example .env
#
# Local dev SQL container only. The SA password must satisfy SQL Server's complexity rules
# (8+ chars, three of: upper / lower / digit / symbol) or the container fails to start.
#
# The value below is a FIXTURE, not a secret, and it is checked in on purpose — decided
# 2026-07-17, when the security audit asked why a plaintext password was sitting in a public
# repo. It authenticates one throwaway container on localhost:1433 that is rebuilt from
# database/backup/CMS.bak on demand, so it grants nothing to anyone who cannot already reach
# this machine's loopback. Replacing it with a placeholder would cost every developer a manual
# step and would not un-publish anything: the repo is public and the value is already in the
# history, which only a force-push could change.
#
# It is literal in two more places — spec/docker-db.md and the http-docker profile in
# src/CMS.API/Properties/launchSettings.json — because launchSettings.json cannot expand
# ${...}. Change one, change all three.
#
# Nothing that guards anything real may join them. docker-compose.yml reads this variable and
# refuses to start without it, so a password that matters goes in .env, which is gitignored.
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=LocalDev#Cms2026

# Host port for the container. The native SQLEXPRESS uses a dynamic port, so 1433 is normally free.
SQL_PORT=1433
